{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:16:26.337Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-brief-yanp"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Replace the future-date empty-window fixture that blocks the PM 2026.10.25 toolchain CI"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-brief#193 (filed 2026-10-28, missed by the blind issue watch). test/coverage-gaps.test.ts:360 (and brief.test.ts since-fixtures) manufacture an empty activity window with the lower bound 2999-01-01; the host activity command rejects --from after --to with invalid_argument_value ('Activity --from must be before --to') once the dev toolchain moves to SDK 2026.10.25 or newer. Main still pins 2026.10.24 and is green, so the defect only surfaces on the pending toolchain bump PR (#192), whose four gates currently fail on it (latest run 41316901703). Fix by replacing the future-date fixture with a bounded past window (or an explicit empty-window construction the host accepts) without weakening the quiet-output assertions; then reland the toolchain update."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","gh:unbraind/pm-brief#193","toolchain"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:16:26.337Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:16:26.337Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"90a4